  message: "Fixed in PR (dev 5421db2471).\n\nBehavioral evidence: the item's repro re-run on merged dev with `hypergumbo verify-claims <repo> --claims claims.yaml --format json` (claims: SECRET-NOT-LOGGED taint_flow host_secret -> logging; NO-LOGGING boundary logging must_not_exist):\n  scala `val k = System.getenv(\"API_KEY\"); println(k)`          -> SECRET-NOT-LOGGED violated, NO-LOGGING violated, exit 1 (filed: both confirmed, no caveat)\n  scala `val k = System.getenv(\"API_KEY\"); Console.err.println(k)` -> both violated, exit 1 (filed: confirmed_with_caveats, untyped_receiver)\nProduction-path tests (test_scala_predef_stdout.py) run verify-claims on nine write shapes: bare println / print / printf, Predef.println, Console.println, Console.err.println, Console.out.print, scala.Console.println, scala.Console.err.println. All nine read violated. Three controls do not read violated: a class's own println; `import acme.io.Console` (inconclusive: an uncatalogued module); a project `object Console`.\n\nFix:\n- scala.yaml now has logging rows for scala.Predef println/print/printf and for scala.Console println/print/printf with attributes out/err, plus an ipc_recv row for Console.in.\n- scala.py: `_scala_static_owner` names the objects `scala._` imports implicitly (Console, Predef) when no import and no project type takes the name.\n- Console.out and Console.err receivers are typed java.io.PrintStream with io_target_kind std_stream, as System.out/err are since WI-rabum. Read as values, they emit module_attr_refs on scala.Console.\n\nCorpus, classified findings vs dev: sbt +179 (159 Predef.println), gatling +20, lila +10. 0 lost, and every addition is logging. An 8-site sbt sample were all real stdout printlns, and no addition sits in sbt's own println-defining ConsoleOut/Terminal files.\n\nGap NOT covered: a bare `println` inside a project class that INHERITS its own println (implicit this) still classifies as Predef's. The placeholder keeps the short-name match beside the linker's resolved edge, the same behaviour as kotlin's ConsoleKt rows. That would be a false violation; none was observed in the sample."  # 3f63
